  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Three rods of material <math> <mi>x</mi> </math> and three rods of material <math> <mi>y</mi> </math> of identical length and cross sectional area&nbsp;are connected as shown in the figure. If the end <math> <mi>A</mi> </math> is maintained at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>60</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup><mtext>C</mtext></math> and the junction <math> <mi>E</mi> </math> at <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mn>10</mn></mrow> <mo>&#8728;</mo> </msup> <mtext>C</mtext></mrow> </math>, then the temperature of junction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is [Given the thermal conductivity of <math> <mi>x</mi> </math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.92</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;and that of <math> <mtext>y</mtext> </math> &nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.46</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>]<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" height=\"136\" src=\"assets\\qt0050_3fb54ddb6601.jpg\" width=\"193\" /></p>\r"
  },
